  "recipe": {
    "technique": "Construction of a fale, especially the large and important fale tele, often involves the whole extended family and help from their village community. The Tufuga fai fale oversees the entire building project. Before construction, the family prepares the building site. Lava, coral, sand or stone materials are usually used for this purpose. The Tufuga, his assistants (autufuga) and men from the family cut the timber from the forest. The main supporting posts, erected first, vary in number, size and length depending on the shape and dimensions of the house.2 m) in the ground. The term for these posts is poutu (standing posts); they are erected in the middle of the house, forming central pillars."
  },
